1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.202
I'm excited to welcome you to this course

2
00:00:02.202 --> 00:00:04.771
on building interactive agents with generative UI,

3
00:00:04.771 --> 00:00:06.473
built in partnership with CopilotKit.

4
00:00:06.473 --> 00:00:09.075
Building a capable AI agent is hard work.

5
00:00:09.075 --> 00:00:11.578
But once you've done that, you get a new challenge:

6
00:00:11.578 --> 00:00:13.313
getting it to users in a

7
00:00:13.313 --> 00:00:15.281
way that they enjoy interacting with it,

8
00:00:15.482 --> 00:00:19.886
which might require much more than building yet another chatbot interface.

9
00:00:20.387 --> 00:00:23.089
Think about what a good agent interface might look like.

10
00:00:23.423 --> 00:00:26.426
Instead of it outputting long paragraphs of text,

11
00:00:26.826 --> 00:00:29.896
maybe the user would rather just get a simple form to fill

12
00:00:29.896 --> 00:00:31.898
or a chart to interact with.

13
00:00:31.998 --> 00:00:34.901
The agent doesn't just answer in plain text,

14
00:00:34.901 --> 00:00:37.904
it can give the user something to see or act on.

15
00:00:38.104 --> 00:00:40.407
In this course, you'll learn to build that interface

16
00:00:40.407 --> 00:00:43.410
using three approaches that generative UI,

17
00:00:43.410 --> 00:00:45.211
where the UI, the user interfaces,

18
00:00:45.412 --> 00:00:49.215
generated. The first approach is controlled components

19
00:00:49.215 --> 00:00:52.218
where you define exactly what the agent can show.

20
00:00:52.852 --> 00:00:55.055
The second is declarative UI

21
00:00:55.255 --> 00:00:57.924
with the framework A2UI,

22
00:00:58.158 --> 00:01:02.629
which is an open spec originated by Google and co-developed with CopilotKit,

23
00:01:03.029 --> 00:01:06.132
where the agent generates layouts from a schema.

24
00:01:06.733 --> 00:01:10.737
The third is open-ended UI with MCP apps, where the agent

25
00:01:11.237 --> 00:01:15.742
surfaces full interactive experiences like whiteboards and approval flows

26
00:01:15.742 --> 00:01:19.446
directly inside your product. Your instructor is Atai Barkai,

27
00:01:19.846 --> 00:01:22.415
who is co-founder of CopilotKit, the team behind

28
00:01:22.415 --> 00:01:25.351
the AG-UI protocol that this course is built on.

29
00:01:25.618 --> 00:01:26.820
Thank you, Andrew.

30
00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:29.222
Every interaction between people and technology

31
00:01:29.222 --> 00:01:31.224
is increasingly mediated by agents.

32
00:01:31.624 --> 00:01:33.593
And yet, as we film this course,

33
00:01:33.626 --> 00:01:35.995
most agents still talk to users in plain text,

34
00:01:36.396 --> 00:01:38.398
which is a lot like the command line

35
00:01:38.431 --> 00:01:40.700
MS-DOS era, of personal computing,

36
00:01:41.234 --> 00:01:44.938
powerful for early adopters but not yet built for mass adoption.

37
00:01:45.338 --> 00:01:47.607
The Windows and Mac era changed that

38
00:01:47.607 --> 00:01:50.243
and brought full-featured applications that anybody could use.

39
00:01:50.844 --> 00:01:52.846
AI is going through the same transition now,

40
00:01:53.546 --> 00:01:55.849
and all UI is becoming AI.

41
00:01:56.149 --> 00:01:59.419
When a user asks for a report, the agent should build it.

42
00:01:59.752 --> 00:02:01.354
When they need to approve something,

43
00:02:01.354 --> 00:02:03.256
the agent should show them a form.

44
00:02:03.556 --> 00:02:06.659
When they need to explore data, the agent should render a chart.

45
00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:09.762
You'll start by connecting a LangChain Deep Agent

46
00:02:09.762 --> 00:02:13.266
to a React front end using CopilotKit and AG-UI.

47
00:02:13.867 --> 00:02:17.270
From there, you'll build across the full generative UI spectrum

48
00:02:17.470 --> 00:02:21.975
from controlled generative UI with handcrafted components that render on demand,

49
00:02:22.375 --> 00:02:24.377
to declarative generative UI

50
00:02:24.477 --> 00:02:28.081
where the agent assembles UIs from a component catalog of building blocks,

51
00:02:28.181 --> 00:02:30.383
to open-ended generative UI.

52
00:02:30.650 --> 00:02:33.520
with app experiences powered first by MCP apps

53
00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:35.522
and then by full app sandboxes.

54
00:02:36.022 --> 00:02:38.124
By the end of this course, you have built

55
00:02:38.124 --> 00:02:41.327
a full-stack agent app that renders charts

56
00:02:41.327 --> 00:02:42.929
and cards on demand,

57
00:02:43.329 --> 00:02:46.833
surfaces a live whiteboard through your custom apps

58
00:02:47.133 --> 00:02:49.068
and keeps a shared to-do list in

59
00:02:49.068 --> 00:02:51.037
sync between the agents and the UI.

60
00:02:51.638 --> 00:02:53.239
CopilotKit is open source,

61
00:02:53.439 --> 00:02:55.608
and it supports all three of the

62
00:02:55.608 --> 00:02:57.810
major generative UI patterns in one framework.

63
00:02:58.411 --> 00:03:01.281
It also has first-party integrations with LangGraph,

64
00:03:01.281 --> 00:03:04.117
Google Cloud, AWS, Microsoft Azure, and others.

65
00:03:04.417 --> 00:03:06.219
Many people have worked to create this course.

66
00:03:06.319 --> 00:03:09.822
I'd like to thank from CopilotKit, Uli Barkai and Tyler Slaton.

67
00:03:10.123 --> 00:03:14.227
From DeepLearning.AI, Summer Rae also worked on this course. In lesson one,

68
00:03:14.327 --> 00:03:16.095
you'll walk through the three major pillars

69
00:03:16.095 --> 00:03:18.131
of the generative UI spectrum side by side.

70
00:03:18.698 --> 00:03:21.401
what makes each one different and when you'd use each one.

71
00:03:22.001 --> 00:03:23.570
By the end, you'll have the mental model

72
00:03:23.570 --> 00:03:25.305
for everything you're going to build in this course.

73
00:03:26.372 --> 00:03:28.942
So, let's jump in and get interactive.
